  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  # Singular uses 4.4.1p5 for the 5th patch release of 4.4.1.\n  # The p is considered as a pre-release version but here it's meant as a patch\n  # release version. This confuses pin_subpackage wich renders\n  # upper_bound=x.x.x.x then as >=4.4.1.0p.5,<4.4.1.1a. Also rattler-build\n  # currently gets these version numbers completely wrong. To make things\n  # easier to handle, we switch to an easier scheme in conda-forge and treat\n  # 4.4.1p5 as 4.4.1.5 which better ressembles the intention by upstream.\n  version: 4.4.1.5\n  name: singular\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/Singular/Singular/releases/download/Release-${{ (version | split('.'))[:-1] | join('-') }}p${{ version | split('.') | last }}/singular-${{ (version | split('.'))[:-1] | join('.') }}p${{ version | split('.') | last }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: b2b328fb19e9f4396dca89ed69929b241f52d2d1b1cc605c17745130a6cd4943\n  patches:\n    - ncursesw.patch\n    - offsetof.patch\n    # Upstream's doc target 'all' also builds DVI files which requires TeX.\n    # We only need the info & HTML docs that upstream ships in doc.tbz2.\n    - docbuild.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  skip: win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: unix\n      then: gnuconfig\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - libtool\n    - automake\n    - autoconf\n    - pkgconf\n    - make\n    - sed\n    - texinfo\n    - perl\n    - bzip2\n  host:\n    - gmp\n    - mpfr\n    - ntl\n    - libflint\n    - cddlib\n    - readline\n    - ncurses\n  run:\n    - gmp\n    - mpfr\n    - ntl\n    - cddlib\n    - readline\n    - ncurses\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('singular', upper_bound='x.x.x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - test -f ${PREFIX}/include/singular/Singular/libsingular.h\n      - test -f ${PREFIX}/lib/libSingular.a\n      - test -f ${PREFIX}/share/info/singular.info\n      - if: osx\n        then: test -f ${PREFIX}/lib/libSingular.dylib\n      - if: linux\n        then: test -f ${PREFIX}/lib/libSingular.so\n\nabout:\n  license: GPL-2.0-or-later\n  license_file: COPYING\n  summary: |\n    Singular is a computer algebra system for polynomial computations, with special emphasis\n    on commutative and non-commutative algebra, algebraic geometry, and singularity theory\n  homepage: https://www.singular.uni-kl.de/\n  repository: https://github.com/Singular/Sources\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - isuruf\n    - saraedum\n",
